 ### [TensoRF Feature Decoding Architecture](8181-tensorf-feature-decoding-architecture.md)
-The TensoRF Feature Decoding Architecture maps compressed feature tensors to radiance and density using ablation-tested linear layer configurations optimized for speed and PSNR, rather than explicit BRDF parameterization. It is distinguished from Neural BRDF and Geometry Decoding by its focus on efficient tensor decoding over explicit material property prediction.
+The TensoRF Feature Decoding Architecture maps compressed feature tensors to radiance and density using ablation-tested linear layer configurations optimized for speed and PSNR, rather than explicit BRDF parameterization. It is distinguished from Neural BRDF and Geometry Decoding by its focus on efficient tensor decoding over explicit material property prediction. Choose it when computational efficiency and standard radiance field reconstruction are prioritized over explicit material relighting.
 
 ### [Neural Surface Rendering](9960-neural-surface-rendering.md)
-Neural Surface Rendering uses a neural shader (MLP) to approximate PBR by mapping geometric attributes (intersection point, normal, view direction) to radiance, learning complex shading effects directly from data. It builds on Neural BRDF and Geometry Decoding by explicitly using surface normals and intersection points as primary inputs for the appearance model [G].
